  "id": "temporal-lobectomy",
  "term": "temporal lobectomy",
  "definition": "Temporal lobectomy, especially anterior temporal lobectomy, is a brain surgery commonly used for drug-resistant temporal lobe epilepsy. In this context, it is relevant to learning and memory because it can be followed by problems with facial memory and face identification.",
